{"title":"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, define the positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /><i>-safe</i> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> differs in absolute value by more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from all multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. For example, the set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-safe numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/6/da6dd3e7c0d249641e8294cd1b2152612dc67a3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 23, \\ldots\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"281\" height=\"18\" />. Find the number of positive integers less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/b/50b19142d92b7b4f1a115c4ec91766582e2b8faf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> which are simultaneously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-safe, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-safe, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-safe.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-safe if and only if the residue of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55c3ee73eb43076fb5edcda7abd70384186a73d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\mod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/1523b5a2cc94318ea1788e9f57c122c869a194a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />; thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/7/5d739fce33991aae44654d6187a71005ceff0fff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> residues <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f965eb9407014fe0e4fc671eed0acbfd84eddb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> that a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-safe number can have. Therefore, a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> satisfying the conditions of the problem can have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> different residues <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/4/5e4461877e328edd4298545f51c7d8d170bd3bed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod 7$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> different residues <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/5/9756fa7ce518774326c7ac638727fd75895d3e94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> different residues <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/0/1305bcbe2070a6c1c0bcfa06102041401e2ee4c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />. The Chinese Remainder Theorem states that for a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> (mod b)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> (mod d)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> (mod f)\nhas one solution if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/b/97bdc1b39487fc39351f7176e150f92e5d14facb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(b,d,f)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"20\" />. For example, in our case, the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can be:\n3 (mod 7)\n3 (mod 11)\n7 (mod 13)\nso since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/f/5ffa7436111db7787ed56e9b666eb238c32bbea1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(7,11,13)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />=1, there is 1 solution for n for this case of residues of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>This means that by the Chinese Remainder Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48c6b6953360d5c30d0af76465046f9958dccaf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 6 \\cdot 8 = 96$\" width=\"95\" height=\"12\" /> different residues mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/c/5fc641915be0dba9364ed5c17ebbcf1886eb1bbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 13 = 1001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"131\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/d/56d48a48117270cb45326e13437bbedbe5b35474.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$960$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> satisfying the conditions in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/a/18ae01e508a365c57cb0765ed3e26d6d2bf9b939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; n \\le 10010$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" />. However, we must now remove any values greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/4/9f4f407fa86791b87ad5286ea377c10b2111d0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> that satisfy the conditions. By checking residues, we easily see that the only such values are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f779b4ed886ae0cece3f20d88fd0e9d0ee98ca0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10006$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/7/ee7fa64c732464732206e79ad10707e9d6884df2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10007$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />, so there remain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/3/c03e64c453fb46c58b6637af7b286878eb15cd67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{958}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"22\" /> values satisfying the conditions of the problem.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<ul><li>We can also say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/726bdcb0779fcb4723bfc790d0f677a9981261a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of all numbers are 7-safe, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/3/063cb9fa3f9c1a13cdde7a7aad39b8464a93424e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> of all numbers are 11-safe, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/d/cbdd6533c2882af567cedd2174829ff136094530.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> of all numbers are 13-safe. We can multiply these to get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/2907df69fb09ebfea6f6da741a897502c69fea18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{96}{1001}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"38\" /> of all numbers are simultaneously 7-safe, 11-safe, and 13-safe.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We want the number of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d47e830cfe8a1c2a43131631324bb3351fcb8f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\le 10000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" /> such that\n\\begin{align*}\nn&amp;\\equiv 3,4\\bmod{7}\\\\\nn&amp;\\equiv 3,4,5,6,7,8,\\bmod{11}\\\\\nn&amp;\\equiv 3,4,5,6,7,8,9,10\\bmod{13}\n\\end{align*}\nBy the Chinese Remainder Theorem, the map\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/d/aadc36f3ae61e1d4a0bda095ee135d7d41695891.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f \\colon \\mathbb{Z}/1001\\mathbb{Z} \\to \\mathbb{Z}/7\\mathbb{Z} \\times \\mathbb{Z}/11\\mathbb{Z} \\times \\mathbb{Z}/13\\mathbb{Z},\\]\" width=\"313\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e46235cf39969cda3eaa2e8852a0469cb35e34d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n \\bmod 1001 \\mapsto (n \\bmod 7, n \\bmod 11, n \\bmod 13)\\]\" width=\"361\" height=\"18\" />\nis bijective. This means that the residues of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> uniquely determine its residue modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888c508062c09735bab7ff0e11e7dc80cc7580db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Hence, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598509bfd07b2f372adbe8b09e45116ad8e6ec0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in [1,10010]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb49a69069f0b98c010e0b5471de759cc93cd05a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\times 6\\times 8\\times 10=960$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"165\" height=\"15\" /> integers that are simultaneously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-safe, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-safe, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-safe.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/7/a87e77f20ef2f547350fd4901197c253e8f3772c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  size(15cm,0); defaultpen(fontsize(8pt));  draw((-0.5,0)--(11.5,0), arrow=Arrow(TeXHead));  int[] reds = {9999, 10000, 10001, 10002, 10003, 10004, 10005, 10008, 10009, 10010}; bool isRed(int n) {     for (int r : reds) if (n == r) return true;     return false; }  for (int i = 0; i &lt;= 11; ++i) {     int n = 9999 + i;     draw((i,0)--(i,0.1));     pen p = isRed(n) ? red : black;     label(Label(string(n), p), (i,0.2), N);     if (n == 9999) {         label(Label(&quot;multiple of 11&quot;), (i,-0.2), S);     }     if (n == 10003) {         label(Label(&quot;multiple of 7&quot;), (i,-0.2), S);     }     if (n == 10010) {         label(Label(&quot;multiple of 7,11,13&quot;), (i,-0.2), S);     } }[/asy]\" width=\"712\" height=\"55\" />\nHowever, this accounts the case when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/6/5c6837d83c807c1d2fcacd4e7a8e3daba96dd3fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=10006,10007$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"17\" />, which are out-of-range. Therefore, the total is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/8/2189ea655d649e41a47fc2bcf8ff37784b9b63a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$960-2=\\boxed{958}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Pieandpi31415926535897932\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II\" title=\"2012 AIME II\">2012 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2012\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2012 AIME II Pro